                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 15,
                "retweet_count": 21,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "\ud83d\udea8The longest government shutdown in American history is officially over. \n\nFor more than six weeks, Democrats held our country hostage over demands for health care for illegal aliens, trillions in wasteful spending, and to prove to their radical base they could 'stand up' to President Trump. The irony? We are in the exact same place with the exact same deal today as we had 43 days ago. \n\nLet me be clear: Democrats gained nothing from their shutdown while hardworking families paid the price. \n\nAfter being home in the district working to ensure my constituents had the resources needed to navigate the chaos and care for their families, I am ready and eager to get back governing and delivering on the mandate we were given by the American people last November.",
                "text_lang": "en",
